IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er5-admin-reconsideration`

-- Tests of er5-admin-reconsideration (regs 78 to 82; regs 83 to 87 are repealed and have no rule). Expected values are written by hand
-- from the text of the Regulations (SOR-96-332.txt lines 1643-1665), beside each assertion, before the run.

§ `Reg 78(1) - what the request must contain (src:1643-1650)`

-- The argument order is: in writing; name; SIN or business number; address and telephone number; has a fax number; the request gives it;
-- has an email address; the request gives it; date the decision was communicated; reasons; has new relevant information; the request contains it.
-- A person with no fax number, no email address and nothing new to add, whose request gives the rest: complete.
#ASSERT `reg 78(1) the request for reconsideration is in writing and contains the information required` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- A person with a fax number and an email address, both given, and new information that is included: complete.
#ASSERT `reg 78(1) the request for reconsideration is in writing and contains the information required` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Not in writing.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 78(1) the request for reconsideration is in writing and contains the information required` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- No name.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 78(1) the request for reconsideration is in writing and contains the information required` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- No social insurance number or business number.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 78(1) the request for reconsideration is in writing and contains the information required` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- No address and telephone number.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 78(1) the request for reconsideration is in writing and contains the information required` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- The person has a fax number and the request leaves it out.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 78(1) the request for reconsideration is in writing and contains the information required` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- The person has an email address and the request leaves it out.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 78(1) the request for reconsideration is in writing and contains the information required` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- No date on which the decision was communicated.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 78(1) the request for reconsideration is in writing and contains the information required` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- No reasons.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 78(1) the request for reconsideration is in writing and contains the information required` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- The person has relevant information not previously provided and the request leaves it out.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 78(1) the request for reconsideration is in writing and contains the information required` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- The person has no such information, so the request need not contain any, even when it says it does not.
#ASSERT `reg 78(1) the request for reconsideration is in writing and contains the information required` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE

§ `Reg 78(2) - where it is filed (src:1651)`

-- The argument order is: the address; the facsimile number; the email address; the electronic filing procedure, each as the Commission's website provides.
#ASSERT `reg 78(2) the request for reconsideration was filed as the Commission's website provides` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 78(2) the request for reconsideration was filed as the Commission's website provides` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 78(2) the request for reconsideration was filed as the Commission's website provides` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 78(2) the request for reconsideration was filed as the Commission's website provides` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Filed some other way (for example, handed to a friend): none of the four.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 78(2) the request for reconsideration was filed as the Commission's website provides` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§ `Reg 79 - the decision without delay (src:1652)`

#ASSERT `reg 79 the Commission must render its decision on the request without delay` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 79 the Commission must render its decision on the request without delay` FALSE)
-- The text gives no measure of delay, so whether the Commission has been too slow is not covered, at any number of days.
#ASSERT `reg 79 the Commission has rendered its decision without delay` 3 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 79 the Commission has rendered its decision without delay` 400 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Reg 80 - the Commission appeals within 21 days (src:1655)`

-- The decision is given on March 1, 2020; 21 days after it is March 22, 2020, which counts (the keel's reading F4).
#ASSERT `reg 80 benefits are not payable in accordance with the decision` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 3 22)) TRUE
-- The appeal is filed on March 23, 2020, the 22nd day: too late.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 80 benefits are not payable in accordance with the decision` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 3 23)) TRUE)
-- An appeal on the day the decision is given (assumed to count).
#ASSERT `reg 80 benefits are not payable in accordance with the decision` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 3 1)) TRUE
-- An appeal dated before the decision cannot be an appeal from it.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 80 benefits are not payable in accordance with the decision` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 2 28)) TRUE)
-- No appeal by the Commission.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 80 benefits are not payable in accordance with the decision` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 1) NOTHING TRUE)
-- The Commission appeals in time on some ground other than an error in law.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 80 benefits are not payable in accordance with the decision` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 3 10)) FALSE)

§ `Reg 81 - the Commission applies for judicial review (src:1656)`

-- The claim is the object of the decision, the Commission has applied, and the application is not yet determined: benefits are not payable.
#ASSERT `reg 81 benefits are not payable in respect of the claim` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- Finally determined: payable again.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 81 benefits are not payable in respect of the claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- The Commission has not applied.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 81 benefits are not payable in respect of the claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- A claim that is not the object of the decision.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 81 benefits are not payable in respect of the claim` FALSE TRUE FALSE)

§ `Reg 82 - a decision that a provision is ultra vires (src:1657-1660)`

-- The claims caught: the claim that is the object of the decision; or a claim made after the decision that would not be payable except for it.
#ASSERT `reg 82(1) and (2) the claim is caught by the decision` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 82(1) and (2) the claim is caught by the decision` FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Made after the decision, but payable anyway.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 82(1) and (2) the claim is caught by the decision` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Not made after the decision, though it would not be payable but for the decision.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 82(1) and (2) the claim is caught by the decision` FALSE FALSE TRUE)

-- Reg 82(1). The argument order is: General Division decision; Board of Appeal decision; the Commission appealed; the claim is caught; the Appeal Division has finally
-- determined the appeal; that determination declares the provision ultra vires; the Commission applied for judicial review; the application is finally determined.
-- A General Division decision under appeal, the appeal not yet determined: not payable.
#ASSERT `reg 82(1) benefits are not payable on the claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- A Board of Appeal decision under appeal, the appeal not yet determined: not payable.
#ASSERT `reg 82(1) benefits are not payable on the claim` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Neither kind of decision.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 82(1) benefits are not payable on the claim` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- The Commission has not appealed.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 82(1) benefits are not payable on the claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- The claim is not caught.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 82(1) benefits are not payable on the claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (a): the Appeal Division has finally determined the appeal and did not declare the provision ultra vires: payable again, even though the Commission has applied for review.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 82(1) benefits are not payable on the claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- (b): the final determination declares the provision ultra vires and the Commission's application for judicial review is pending: still not payable.
#ASSERT `reg 82(1) benefits are not payable on the claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- (b): the application for judicial review is finally determined: payable.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 82(1) benefits are not payable on the claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- The final determination declares the provision ultra vires and the Commission has not applied for judicial review (the reading taken): the stoppage ended at (a).
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 82(1) benefits are not payable on the claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)

-- Reg 82(2). The argument order is: the Appeal Division's decision declares the provision ultra vires; the Commission applied for judicial review; the claim is caught; the application is finally determined.
#ASSERT `reg 82(2) benefits are not payable on the claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 82(2) benefits are not payable on the claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 82(2) benefits are not payable on the claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 82(2) benefits are not payable on the claim` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 82(2) benefits are not payable on the claim` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)

§ `Regs 83 to 87 - repealed (src:1661-1665)`

-- The stub is documentation with a section number; it decides nothing. A chain of string literals evaluates to the inert TRUE, which is all that is asserted.
#ASSERT `regs 83 to 87 are repealed and therefore not encoded`
